{"cve": "CVE-2026-41583", "version": "N/A", "published": "2026-05-08T15:16:41.070", "lastModified": "2026-05-08T18:44:58.830", "description": "ZEBRA is a Zcash node written entirely in Rust. Prior to zebrad version 4.3.1 and prior to zebra-script version 5.0.2, after a refactoring, Zebra failed to validate a consensus rule that restricted the possible values of sighash hash types for V5 transactions which were enabled in the NU5 network upgrade. Zebra nodes could thus accept and eventually mine a block that would be considered invalid by zcashd nodes, creating a consensus split between Zebra and zcashd nodes. In a similar vein, for V4 transactions, Zebra mistakenly used the \"canonical\" hash type when computing the sighash while zcashd (correctly per the spec) uses the raw value, which could also crate a consensus split. This issue has been patched in zebrad version 4.3.1 and zebra-script version 5.0.2.", "cvssScore": 9.1, "cvsseSeverity": "CRITICAL", "CWE": ["573", "710"], "CAPEC": [], "TECHNIQUES": [], "DEFEND": []}
{"cve": "CVE-2026-44497", "version": "N/A", "published": "2026-05-08T15:17:01.493", "lastModified": "2026-05-08T18:42:24.100", "description": "ZEBRA is a Zcash node written entirely in Rust. Prior to zebrad version 4.4.0 and prior to zebra-script version 6.0.0, the fix for CVE-2026-41583 introduced a separate issue due to insufficient error handling of the case where the sighash type is invalid, during sighash computation. Instead of returning an error, the normal flow would resume, and the input sighash buffer would be left untouched. In scenarios where a previous signature validation could leave a valid sighash in the buffer, an invalid hash-type could be incorrectly accepted, which would create a consensus split between Zebra and zcashd nodes. This issue has been patched in zebrad version 4.4.0 and zebra-script version 6.0.0.", "cvssScore": 9.1, "cvsseSeverity": "CRITICAL", "CWE": ["345", "347", "693"], "CAPEC": ["111", "665", "57", "107", "22", "477", "59", "218", "237", "142", "20", "386", "148", "388", "87", "475", "463", "701", "127", "385", "141", "668", "17", "74", "480", "65", "51", "387", "1", "384", "36"], "TECHNIQUES": [{"id": "1040", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1083", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1211", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1491", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1542.002", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1556", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1557.002", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1565.002", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1574.005", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1574.010", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1584.002", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}, {"id": "1611", "name": "ENTRY NAME", "tactics": []}], "DEFEND": [{"id": "D3-DNSTA", "tactic": "Detect", "technique": "DNS Traffic Analysis", "artifact": "DNS Lookup"}, {"id": "D3-FA", "tactic": "Detect", "technique": "File Analysis", "artifac